(2) the dodge: on a hiding-interval J (width delta) in t, the extremity set X={a<1/12,b>5/12}∪sym is
    a union of boxes of width <= 1/(6 min(w1,w2)); if delta exceeds the box+gap scale, J has a
    non-extremity point => M>=1/12. LARGE tighteners: boxes tiny, trivial. SMALL tighteners: need delta big.
    (opus proved the delta=0 point-only AP case; loose U has delta>0 => interval room.)
